						<p>16 May: the vector-memory era. <code>brain_experience</code>, <code>brain_context</code> and <code>brain_reflection</code> arrive — closed trades become 768D embeddings in ChromaDB, retrievable before the next decision, with a reflection pass that writes rules in plain language. A few days earlier (12 May) came the blunt commit message "make bot profitable with Gemini Flash 3 Preview" — that one aged badly, and I left it in the history on purpose.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="timeline-item">
